# GitHub squash merge commit subjects

When squash-merging a pull request with `gh pr merge --squash`:

- Set `--subject` to the PR title (or a short imperative summary) **plus the PR number in parentheses**.
- Format: `type(scope): short description (#123)`
- Subject only — no commit body unless the user explicitly asks for one.
- Use `--delete-branch` unless told otherwise.

Examples:

- `fix(core): add maintenance mode and recovery scripts (#112)`
- `fix: secure production and stabilize previews (#110)`
- `feat: platform v1 epic (#111)`

Do not omit `(#PR)` from squash merge subjects.
